  "concepts": [
    {
      "id": "ST-HOOKS",
      "title": {
        "en": "Give every slow segment a reason to stay"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Restructure the illustrative grind using the agency segment rules."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "A [[T-ST-HOOK]] states why an audience should keep watching the current [[T-ST-SEGMENT]]. A [[T-ST-ROS]] names each [[T-ST-SEGMENT]], its goal and its target duration."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §2-3, LW-3.1; §5, LW-5.1 and LW-5.2; scenario segments"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "In the illustrative case, the silent grind [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] ran from minute 38 to minute 60 with no stated goal or chat interaction. The agency rule LW-5.2 limits a grind [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] to 10 minutes with a stated goal and audience participation. The weak [[T-ST-HOOK]] and missing participation are review hypotheses; the chart alone does not prove why each viewer left."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §2-3, LW-3.1; §5, LW-5.1 and LW-5.2; scenario segments"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "Review the [[T-ST-VOD]] around the transition before diagnosing the [[T-ST-SEGMENT]]. Draft a shorter grind [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] with a stated goal and a poll, following the agency playbook. Save the revised [[T-ST-ROS]] for the manager instead of changing the live stream automatically."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §2-3, LW-3.1; §5, LW-5.1 and LW-5.2; scenario segments"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "A slow [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] needs a [[T-ST-HOOK]] and a plan under this agency playbook. Treat the duration and silence limits as agency rules, not universal platform statistics."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §2-3, LW-3.1; §5, LW-5.1 and LW-5.2; scenario segments"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-HOOKS-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ST-CHAT",
      "title": {
        "en": "Read chat as an early warning, then verify"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Compare the timing of chat and viewer changes without claiming causation from correlation."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "The [[T-ST-CHAT]] is the number of messages per minute in this case. A [[T-ST-MECHANIC]] gives viewers a planned way to participate, such as a poll."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, LW-4.1; scenario drop and series.chatPerMin"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "The case [[T-ST-CHAT]] fell from 87 messages at minute 37 to 15 at minute 41. The viewer line remained near its earlier level around minute 40 before declining. The agency treats [[T-ST-CHAT]] as an early warning, but a quiet chat alone cannot identify a cause."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, LW-4.1; scenario drop and series.chatPerMin"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "Under the agency rule LW-4.1, every grind or loading stretch needs a [[T-ST-MECHANIC]]. Compare [[T-ST-CHAT]] with the [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] transition, then inspect the [[T-ST-VOD]] to check what changed. Record the warning and the proposed response in the next plan; do not infer a live audience preference from one signal."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, LW-4.1; scenario drop and series.chatPerMin"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "Use [[T-ST-CHAT]] with the viewer line and [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] notes. Treat a missing [[T-ST-MECHANIC]] as a playbook gap, while keeping the causal diagnosis provisional."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §4, LW-4.1; scenario drop and series.chatPerMin"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-CHAT-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ST-RETENTION",
      "title": {
        "en": "Compare segments without mistaking counts for people"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Compute the agency segment ratio and explain its limits."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "The [[T-ST-CCV]] measures concurrent viewers at a moment, rather than unique viewers across the whole stream. The agency defines [[T-ST-RETENTION]] as last-minute [[T-ST-CCV]] divided by first-minute [[T-ST-CCV]]."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.1; scenario segmentStats, series and drop"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "The case grind [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] uses minute 38 as its first sample and minute 59 as its last, with [[T-ST-CCV]] of 556 and 348. The [[T-ST-RETENTION]] is about 0.626, rounded to 0.63, below the agency review threshold of 0.8. This ratio compares counts; it does not prove that the same 63% of viewers stayed throughout."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.1; scenario segmentStats, series and drop"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "The case vote [[T-ST-SEGMENT]] has [[T-ST-CCV]] of 351 at minute 60 and 477 at minute 91, giving a ratio near 1.36. A [[T-ST-RETENTION]] above 1 indicates net growth in concurrent counts, not impossible individual retention. Under the agency rule LW-6.1, flag the grind for [[T-ST-VOD]] review and keep the later raid separate from this comparison."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.1; scenario segmentStats, series and drop"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "Always state the [[T-ST-CCV]] endpoint convention when reporting [[T-ST-RETENTION]]. Use the agency threshold to prioritise review, rather than to assert a causal explanation."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.1; scenario segmentStats, series and drop"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-RETENTION-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-line"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ST-EXPERIMENT",
      "title": {
        "en": "Propose one change and a measurable review"
      },
      "goal": {
        "en": "Write a single-change learning plan with a prediction, measure and attribution limits."
      },
      "placards": [
        {
          "kind": "definition",
          "text": {
            "en": "An [[T-ST-EXPERIMENT]] records a planned change, the expected effect and a measure for review. A [[T-ST-CONFOUNDER]] is another changing factor that makes attribution uncertain."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.2; §5, LW-5.1; scenario recovery and events"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-experiment-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "concept",
          "text": {
            "en": "Under the agency rule LW-6.2, change one thing per stream and log the prediction, measure and result. The case recovery coincided with polls, talking and a new [[T-ST-SEGMENT]], so it cannot isolate one change. The incoming raid at minute 95 is another [[T-ST-CONFOUNDER]] when comparing later viewer counts."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.2; §5, LW-5.1; scenario recovery and events"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-experiment-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "application",
          "text": {
            "en": "Draft one [[T-ST-EXPERIMENT]] that adds a poll to an otherwise comparable slow [[T-ST-SEGMENT]]. Keep the goal and duration fixed, then compare [[T-ST-RETENTION]] and [[T-ST-CHAT]] while logging audience-source differences. State a provisional review threshold before the next stream, send the plan to the manager, and record an inconclusive result honestly."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.2; §5, LW-5.1; scenario recovery and events"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-experiment-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "recap",
          "text": {
            "en": "A useful [[T-ST-EXPERIMENT]] includes one change, a prediction, a measure and a review decision. A threshold guides review; a positive result does not remove every [[T-ST-CONFOUNDER]] or prove causation."
          },
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-PLAYBOOK",
              "title": "Launch-week streaming playbook (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/playbook-excerpt.md; §6, LW-6.2; §5, LW-5.1; scenario recovery and events"
            },
            {
              "id": "S-ST-EXPERIMENT-CASE",
              "title": "Launch-week stream case (illustrative)",
              "locator": "content/knowledge-workers/sources/design/personas/streamer/scenario.json"
            }
          ],
          "sceneId": "st-experiment-flow"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "terms": [
    {
      "id": "T-ST-HOOK",
      "term": "hook",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "A stated reason for the audience to keep watching.",
        "hi-Latn": "Viewer ko rukne ka saaf reason."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "hook"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-SEGMENT",
      "term": "segment",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "A named block of a stream with a goal and planned duration.",
        "hi-Latn": "Stream ka naam aur goal wala time block."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "segment"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-ROS",
      "term": "run-of-show",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "The ordered plan of named segments and target durations.",
        "hi-Latn": "Segments ka order, goal aur planned time."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "run of show"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-VOD",
      "term": "VOD",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "The saved video recording used to review what happened on stream.",
        "hi-Latn": "Stream ki saved recording jise review karte hain."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "V O D"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-CHAT",
      "term": "chat rate",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "Messages per minute in this illustrative analytics case.",
        "hi-Latn": "Is case mein ek minute ke chat messages."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "chat rate"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-MECHANIC",
      "term": "chat mechanic",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "A planned way for viewers to participate, such as a poll.",
        "hi-Latn": "Viewers ko involve karne ka planned tareeka, jaise poll."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "chat mechanic"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-CCV",
      "term": "CCV",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "Concurrent viewers at a given time, rather than unique people across the whole stream.",
        "hi-Latn": "Ek waqt par dekh rahe viewers; poore stream ke unique log nahi."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "C C V"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-RETENTION",
      "term": "segment retention",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "The agency ratio of last-minute CCV to first-minute CCV in a segment.",
        "hi-Latn": "Agency ka ratio: segment ke last minute ka CCV, first minute ke CCV se divide."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "segment retention"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-EXPERIMENT",
      "term": "experiment",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "A planned change with a prediction and a measure for the next review.",
        "hi-Latn": "Ek planned change, expected effect aur measure ke saath."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "experiment"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "T-ST-CONFOUNDER",
      "term": "confounder",
      "meaning": {
        "en": "Another changing factor that makes attribution of a result uncertain.",
        "hi-Latn": "Doosra badalta factor jo result ka reason clear nahi hone deta."
      },
      "say": {
        "hi-Latn": "confounder"
      }
    }
  ],
